  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consultation on South Sudan&apos;s Disaster Risk Management Bill at the National and Sub-National level</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project feeds into the World Bank funded programme Enhancing Community Resilience and Local Governance Project Phase II (ECRP-II) that aims to improve access to services, strengthen flood resilience, and enhance institutional capacity for local service delivery and integrated disaster risk management at the national and sub-national levels. It does so by complementing component 2 of ECRP-II programme that encompassed Disaster Risk Management (DRM) capacity building and institutional strengthening at the community, county, and national/state level. In alignment with the priorities set out in South Sudan&apos;s National Disaster Risk Management Policy, the project activities aim to strengthen DRM governance structures and enhance coordination across various levels of government and policy domains through: a) Providing technical and facilitation support to the Ministry of Humanitarian Affairs and Disaster Management to conduct stakeholders Consultations at the National and State Level for the Disaster Risk Management Bill; and b) Provide technical expertise in the review of policies and governance arrangements for DRM, including: an overview of sector policies and governance arrangements for DRM at the national, state level and county level, map existing DRM interventions, identifying ongoing and planned policy or legal instruments and indicate priority needs for policy and institutional capacity development support. 
 
For this particular interventions, IOM is working in partnership with the Ministry of Humanitarian Affairs and Disaster Management (MHADM) and the Relief and Rehabilitation Commission (RRC) at national and field level. The MHADM is key government actor in charge of the implementation of the National Disaster Risk Management Policy (2021). The MHADM prepared the National Disaster Risk Reduction Strategy for 2019-24 in accordance with National DRM Policy and have the mandate to implement and monitor the strategy implementation in collaboration with Relief and Rehabilitation Commission (RRC). The MHADM also work with Commission for Refugee Affairs (CRA) and Ministry of Peace Building.</narrative>
  </description>
